Conformance
Id	Clause
conformance.1	This module specification describes the module that supplies the schema of what a model is given and generates in the Anthropic Messages API [ANTHROPIC-API], as the beta types of the Anthropic Python SDK write it [ANTHROPIC-SDK], to the module that reads a recording of it. It is a module specification of the living-memory specification, and restates nothing that specification states.
conformance.2	The key words "MUST", "MUST NOT", "REQUIRED", "SHALL", "SHALL NOT", "SHOULD", "SHOULD NOT", "RECOMMENDED", "NOT RECOMMENDED", "MAY", and "OPTIONAL" in this specification are to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 [BCP14] when, and only when, they appear in all capitals, as shown here.
conformance.3	The Rules are normative. Each rule states one requirement, and its Id names what it governs and the requirement's number: kept, what the module supplies and leaves out; schema, how the schema is derived. This specification has no optional features.
conformance.4	An implementation of this module conforms if it meets every rule; each rule's test assertion is a test of the implementation, named by the rule's Id.
Rules
Id	Rule
kept.1	The model is given the prior conversational turns as input messages and generates the next message; the system prompt gives it context and instructions; tools are the tools it may use [ANTHROPIC-API]. The model's response is its content, it ends by stop_reason, stop_sequence and stop_details, and input_transformations and context_management report what the API changed in the input before showing it to the model [ANTHROPIC-SDK]. The module MUST supply the schema of these parts only: a request's system, tools and messages, and a response's content, stop_reason, stop_sequence, stop_details, input_transformations and context_management; the request's other members, its controls, and the response's other members are not kept.
kept.2	cache_control creates a cache control breakpoint at its content block [ANTHROPIC-API], an instruction about delivery; the module MUST leave it out of the schema and out of every unit it supplies, from each system block, tool and content block, and from each block that a block's content, or its source's content, holds.
schema.1	A beta request adds members to the request and content blocks to its messages, among them tool_addition [ANTHROPIC-SDK]. The schema MUST be derived type by type from the SDK's beta types, for the kept parts only (kept.1, kept.2), into a JSON Schema of draft-07 [JSON-SCHEMA-07].
schema.2	The SDK writes each type as a Python class or alias [PEP484]. A TypedDict, written as a class or by its alternative syntax [PEP589], MUST be an object whose required keys are those marked Required, or all of them where it is total [PEP655].
schema.3	A BaseModel MUST be an object whose required fields are those without a default.
schema.4	Union MUST be anyOf, Optional anyOf with null, Literal an enum [PEP586], Iterable, List and Sequence an array of their items, Dict[str, X] an object of X, and object any value [PEP484].
schema.5	An alternative no JSON text can hold, a file or a path the SDK reads before sending, MUST be left out, a JSON value being only false, null, true, an object, an array, a number or a string [RFC8259].
schema.6	TYPE_CHECKING is true during type checking and false at run time [PEP484]; a definition under if TYPE_CHECKING MUST be the one read, as a type checker reads it.
schema.7	Each named type MUST be a definition reached by $ref [JSON-SCHEMA-07], named by its type's name where its package exports it, else by its module's name, '.', and its name.
schema.8	Each definition MUST cite the file that defines it.
schema.9	Each object MUST be left open, so a member newer than the SDK's commit is kept, as omitting additionalProperties allows every member [JSON-SCHEMA-07].
schema.10	The schema is a generated file, and MUST be generated from the SDK's type files at the commit its reference cites [ANTHROPIC-SDK], by the generator the implementation holds.
schema.11	The schema MUST say at its start that it is generated.
